# Environment variables for the enquiry email.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or set the same names in the Netlify dashboard
# under Site configuration -> Environment variables, with the Functions
# scope). `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Three transports are supported, tried in this order:
#   1. the Zoho Mail API  (needs a paid plan to reach external recipients)
#   2. SMTP over TLS      (works on a free plan - needs a Zoho app password)
#   3. the Resend API     (needs a verified sending domain)
#
# Set up whichever one you have. The function uses the first that is
# configured, and falls through to the next if one fails.

# --- Zoho Mail API (used when present) ---
# From https://api-console.zoho.com -> Add Client -> Server-based Application.
# The refresh token does not expire, so nothing here needs rotating.
# ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=1000.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
# ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN=1000.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# The account id is optional - the function fetches it if it is not set.
# ZOHO_ACCOUNT_ID=1234567890
# A European Zoho account is "eu", not "us". A token from the wrong region
# is rejected with "invalid_client".
# ZOHO_REGION=eu
# ZOHO_FROM_EMAIL=you@example.com
# ZOHO_FROM_NAME=Pliva River Lodge

# --- Zoho SMTP (used when the API above is not configured) ---
# Needs an app-specific password: Zoho Mail -> Settings -> Mailboxes ->
# the mailbox -> Edit -> App passwords -> Generate. It is 12 characters and
# is shown only once.
#
# The host depends on the kind of account:
#   smtppro.zoho.com  a PAID account on a custom domain
#   smtp.zoho.com     a personal account, or a free organisation account
# Using the wrong one does NOT fail loudly - the server answers
# "535 5.7.8 Authentication Failed", which looks exactly like a wrong
# password. The transport tries the sibling host automatically when that
# happens, so getting it wrong is no longer a dead end.
#
# The From address must be one the mailbox may send as. Zoho refuses to
# relay for anything else with "550 5.7.1 Sender is not allowed to relay".
#
# SMTP_USER is the mailbox that LOGS IN - keep it as the account that owns
# the app password. An alias cannot authenticate.
# SMTP_FROM_EMAIL is the address the guest SEES, and it MAY be an email
# alias created on that same Zoho account (Admin Console -> Users -> the
# account -> Mailbox Settings -> Email Alias). The alias's domain needs
# its own SPF and DKIM, or the mail is treated as spoofed.
# Check an address before using it:
#   node tools/smtp-from-check.mjs guesthouse@yourdomain.com
# SMTP_HOST=smtppro.zoho.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=you@example.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-zoho-app-password
# SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=you@example.com
# SMTP_SECURE=ssl
# SMTP_FROM_NAME=Pliva River Lodge

# --- Resend HTTP API (used when neither of the above is configured) ---
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Who receives the enquiry ---
# MAIL_TO=milkasobic25@gmail.com
# The collaborator is blind-copied, never copied, so Milka can forward an
# enquiry without exposing that address.
# MAIL_BCC=francesco.capuzzo@zoho.com
# MAIL_FROM=Pliva River Lodge <bookings@plivariverlodge.com>

# --- Other ---
# JWT_SECRET=change-me
